{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam al-Baqir (a.s.)",
  "data": "سُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ وَلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI WAL HAMDU LILLAAHI WA LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WALLAAHU AKBAR\nAll glory be to Allah, all praise be to Allah, there is no god save Allah, and Allah is the Greatest.\nUpon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْاَلُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA\nO Allah, I beseech You,\nيَا حَلِيْمُ ذُوْ اَنَاةٍ\nYAA HALEEMU DHOO ANAATIN\nO Indulgent, Forbearing,\nغَفُوْرٌ وَدُوْدٌ\nGHAFOORUN WADOOD\nForgiving, and Loving-kind,\nاَنْ تَتَجَاوَزَ عَنْ سَيِّئَاتِيْ وَمَا عِنْدِيْ\nAN TATAJAAWAZA A'N SAYYI'AATEE WA MAA I'NDEE\nto overlook my sins and what I have had,\nبِحُسْنِ مَا عِنْدَكَ\nBIHUSNI MAA I'NDAK\nout of the excellence of what You have,\nوَاَنْ تُعْطِيَنِيْ مِنْ عَطَائِكَ مَا يَسَعُنِيْ\nWA AN TU'TIYANEE MIN A'TAA'IKA MAA YASA'UNEE\nto give me, out of Your giving, that which suffices me,\nوَتُلْهِمَنِيْ فيمَا اَعْطَيْتَنِيْ الْعَمَلَ فيهِ\nWA TULHIMANEE FEEMAA A'TAYTANIL A'MALA FEEH\nto inspire me to act upon what You have given me;\nبِطَاعَتِكَ وَطَاعَةِ رَسُوْلِكَ\nBITAA'ATIKA WA TAA'ATI RASOOLIK\nthat is to obey You and to obey Your Messenger,\nوَاَنْ تُعْطِيَنِيْ مِنْ عَفْوِكَ\nWA AN TU'TIYANEE MIN A'FWIK\nand to give me part of Your pardon\nمَا اَسْتَوْجِبُ بِهٖ كَرَامَتَكَ\nMAA ASTAWJIBU BIHEE KARAAMATAK\nso much so that I ought to have Your honoring.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَعْطِنِيْ مَا اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ\nALLAAHUMMA A'TINEE MAA ANTA AHLUH\nO Allah, (please) grant me that which befits You\nوَلَا تَفْعَلْ بِيْ مَا اَنَا اَهْلُهٗ\nWA LAA TAF'AL BEE MAA ANAA AHLUH\nand do not do to me that which I deserve.\nفَاِنَّمَا اَنَا بِكَ\nFA-INNAMAA ANAA BIK\nVerily, I exist through You\nوَلَمْ اُصِبْ خَيْراً قَطُّ اِلَّا مِنْكَ\nWA LAM USIB KHAYRAN QATTU ILLAA MINK\nand I have never been given any good thing from any source except You.\nيَا اَبْصَرَ الْاَبْصَرِيْنَ\nYAA ABSARAL ABSAREEN\nO He Who is the best Seer of all those who can see!\nوَيَا اَسْمَعَ السَّامِعِيْنَ\nWA YAA ASMA'AS SAAMI'EEN\nO He Who is the best Hearer of all those who can hear!\nوَيَا اَحْكَمَ الْحَاكِمِيْنَ\nWA YAA AHKAMAL HAAKIMEEN\nO He Who is the Justest of all those who judge!\nوَيَا جَارَ الْمُسْتَجِيْرِيْنَ\nWA YAA JAARAL MUSTAJEEREEN\nO He Who aids those who seek His aid!\nوَيَا مُجِيْبَ دَعْوَةِ الْمُضْطَرِّيْنَ\nWA YAA MUJEEBA DA'WATIL MUDTARREEN\nO He Who responds to the prayer of the oppressed!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nSend blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has recorded a special prayer and supplication for each of the Holy Imams (a.s.), to be offered on Fridays.\nImam al-Baqir (a.s.)'s prayer consists of two units. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and then repeat the following litany one hundred times."
}
